$\begin{align}
&\phantom{=}\dfrac{x^4+3x^3-10x^2}{x^2-2x}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{x^2(x-2)(x+5)}{x(x-2)}\qquad\gray{\text{Factor numerator & denominator}}
\\\\
&=\dfrac{x\cdot \cancel {x}\cancel{(x-2)}(x+5)}{\cancel {x}\cancel{(x-2)}}\qquad\gray{\text{Cancel out common factors}}
\\\\
&=x^2+5x, \text{ for }x\neq 0,2
\end{align}$
